  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates a hybrid classical–quantum neural network (FH:NN/VC‑DRC) for SME credit scoring on a Singapore dataset of ~2,246 firms using a PennyLane simulator with up to 18 qubits. The hybrid model achieves ROC‑AUC ≈0.75 after 350 epochs, compared with ≈0.73 for a classical neural network trained for 350 epochs and ≈0.75 when the classical model is trained longer (≈3500–5000 epochs). Thus the quantum model reaches comparable accuracy with fewer epochs but does not outperform classical methods.",
